Source of motanka-qt6 and motanka-qt6-dev: Qt 6.12.0 (qtbase,
qtshadertools, qtsvg, qtdeclarative, qtwayland, qtimageformats) under
/opt/motanka, for Ubuntu 24.04 and 26.04. Upstream's desktop shell declares
`var native = ...` in QML, which Qt accepts from 6.11 on; both archives
carry Qt 6.10, so the Stack ships its own Qt on both releases
(requirement 1.2; design.md, "Qt for both releases"). When a release's
archive has Qt 6.11 or later, that release can go back to it.

The upstream tarballs are listed in stack/qt6-components.tsv (imported by
build-imports). test/vm/build downloads and verifies them with
stack/fetch-sources --components stack/qt6-components.tsv and passes them
to packaging/build.sh as dpkg-source 3.0 (quilt) orig-<component>
tarballs.

Per release:
  noble     GCC 16 from the Ubuntu toolchain PPA (sbuild-repos), at build
            time only. GCC 16's libstdc++ and libgcc_s come from
            motanka-stack-libs in /opt/motanka/lib, so motanka-qt6 depends
            on it (debian/rules sets ${motanka:Depends}).
  resolute  the archive's GCC 16 and C++ runtime; nothing is bundled and
            motanka-qt6 depends on the archive's libstdc++6.
Both: every ELF has RUNPATH /opt/motanka/lib only. Qt derives its plugin
and QML folders from the location of libQt6Core, so they are
/opt/motanka/lib/qt6/plugins and /opt/motanka/lib/qt6/qml; Ubuntu's Qt in
/usr is never searched. No ld.so.conf.d entry and no LD_LIBRARY_PATH.

Image formats (qtimageformats): WebP and TIFF against the archive's
libwebp and libtiff, plus ICNS, TGA and WBMP; no JPEG 2000 and no MNG.
qtbase adds JPEG, GIF, ICO and PNG; qtsvg adds SVG. The resolute build
requires the archive's libwebp; on noble Qt falls back to its bundled
libwebp if it rejects 24.04's 1.3, and the build log names the one used.

Packages:
  motanka-qt6      libraries (/opt/motanka/lib/libQt6*.so.*), plugins and
                   QML modules (/opt/motanka/lib/qt6/{plugins,qml}).
  motanka-qt6-dev  headers, CMake and pkg-config files, tools, mkspecs and
                   static helper libraries. Build time only: its control
                   carries "Motanka-Build-Only: yes", chumak/build-repo
                   leaves it out of every suite, and packaging/build.sh gives
                   it to the motanka-stack-shell build through sbuild
                   --extra-package (packaging/motanka-stack-shell/sbuild-local).

Build order on noble: packaging/motanka-stack (for motanka-stack-libs, which
the shell build installs as a dependency of motanka-qt6), then
packaging/motanka-qt6, then packaging/motanka-stack-shell. On resolute:
packaging/motanka-qt6, then packaging/motanka-stack-shell.
